abstract: "A book that builds two measures of freedom from two assumptions (no one has perfect knowledge; mistakes are inevitable), computes what raises and lowers a person on both, and prices the lowering. Every claim is tagged as proven, exact, simulated, data or conjecture. The repository holds the text, every script, every results file, a command that re-runs the computations and checks each number against the book, and a schedule calculator that runs on the reader's own device."
keywords:
  - agency
  - information theory
  - schedule instability
  - reproducible research
